      "default": "High-gluten flour + low-gluten flour 1:1 = all-purpose flour;\nHigh-gluten flour + cornstarch 4:1 = all-purpose flour;\nAll-purpose flour + cornstarch 4:1 = cake flour;\nHigh-gluten flour + cornstarch 1:1 = cake flour\nAll-purpose flour can also increase gluten strength by adding vital wheat gluten, but the specific ratio will vary depending on different brands."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "flour_q2",
      "label": "Flour Classification Question",
      "default": "Question 034: What are the main classifications of flour?"
    },
